 Now hold it.

243
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,340
 The Tenth of Thermidor.

244
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:58,160
 Bet you I'll be replacing that man.

245
00:24:01,980 --> 00:24:04,110
 At least I wasn't talking about that one there.

246
00:24:05,470 --> 00:24:10,490
 The fall from power of Robespierre and his friends marked the end of the reign of terror.

247
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:13,830
 A new dance was the rage of Paris, the waltz.

248
00:24:13,830 --> 00:24:19,880
 More than 600 balls were given that year, each one attended by marvelous and incredible women.

249
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:24,520
 Divorce had just been legalized, and it too was all the rage.

250
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:28,050
 Oh, I'm a darling.

251
00:24:28,230 --> 00:24:32,950
 Theresa, here I'd like you to meet my latest husband, the citizen le tenueuse, my good friend Theresa.

252
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,550
 Congratulations, you both know Barav.

253
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:40,750
 Monsieur, I'm sorry to disturb you.

254
00:24:40,910 --> 00:24:43,730
 A messenger has just arrived and he insists that it's very serious.

255
00:24:43,850 --> 00:24:46,550
 It was just announced to Barav that there was a royalist insurrection.

256
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:50,610
 Since the little Bonaparte was not on active duty anyway and relaxing in the salon.

257
00:24:50,610 --> 00:24:53,280
 We are sure to trust you in this urgent business and try to show yourself worthy.

258
00:24:55,500 --> 00:25:00,600
 So with 40 well-placed cannons, the young Bonaparte crushed the final hopes of the royalists.

259
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:04,720
 But Paris knew only misery and hunger. Inflation soared.

260
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:08,100
 A pity on a poor rich man, dear madame. Thank you.

261
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:15,550
 Introducing my very last husband, the Citizen Abou.

262
00:25:16,270 --> 00:25:19,410
 The bread ration fell as low as 60 grams a day.

263
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:27,230
 Possible. It wasn't worth the trouble to have the ration to end where we are.

264
00:25:28,050 --> 00:25:32,930
 Grab all the bread. Come on. Let people out.

265
00:25:35,820 --> 00:25:39,420
 Yes, what the directory needed was a clear-minded man.

266
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:41,280
 A strong one to straighten things out.

267
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:42,860
 A man sent by Providence.

268
00:25:43,380 --> 00:25:45,380
 But let us return to Madame Tallien's salon.

269
00:25:45,530 --> 00:25:49,330
 Happiness with her husband didn't last long and she was much taken with Bonaparte,

270
00:25:49,470 --> 00:25:52,130
 but she tired soon enough of a little general with no future,

271
00:25:52,430 --> 00:25:56,930
 who at any rate was more interested in the ravishing Josephine, who Barra was now tired of.

272
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:59,980
 Bonaparte falls madly in love, wants to marry her, but he's penniless.

273
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:04,480
 Josephine didn't exactly say no and would be interested if her general had a little position.

274
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:06,560
 Barra, head of the army, makes a gesture.

275
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:08,920
 He gives Bonaparte the little army in Italy.

276
00:26:09,290 --> 00:26:13,440
 Whatever the outcome, nobody expected much from him, but much was to happen indeed.

277
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:18,130
 Yes, France was greatly involved.

278
00:26:18,130 --> 00:26:21,070
 The European nations didn't get along for a century.

279
00:26:37,030 --> 00:26:42,150
 Long before the collective suicide of 1914, from which two giants emerged, Napoleon was

280
00:26:42,150 --> 00:26:47,350
 to say, as I die, I leave two giants yet in their cradles to revenge me, Russia and the

281
00:26:47,350 --> 00:26:48,410
 United States of America.

